    {
      "title": "Strategy, State and Template Method",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strategy, State and Template Method",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strategy and State",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Strategy}: client picks ==one algorithm object== behind one interface",
                "Context delegates; strategies never know each other",
                "e.g. sort comparator, payment method, compression",
                "{green:State}: context holds a ==current state== and delegates",
                "States replace the context's state themselves",
                "e.g. TCP Open/Closed, Order Pending/Shipped"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Strategy",
                "State"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Class diagram",
                  "identical",
                  "identical"
                ],
                [
                  "Chosen by",
                  "**client**",
                  "the object itself"
                ],
                [
                  "Over time",
                  "stays fixed",
                  "changes automatically"
                ],
                [
                  "Know each other",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Template Method",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Base class: a ==final method== is the skeleton",
                "It calls {red:abstract steps} and optional {green:hooks}",
                "Subclasses override ==steps only==",
                "**Hollywood principle**: the base calls you, you don't call it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Parser(ABC):",
                "    def parse(self):  # skeleton, not overridden",
                "        self.open()",
                "        data = self.extract()",
                "        self.close()",
                "        return data"
              ],
              "note": "open and extract are abstract steps"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Template Method vs Strategy",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Template Method",
                "Strategy"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Varies",
                  "parts of one algorithm",
                  "the whole algorithm"
                ],
                [
                  "Mechanism",
                  "inheritance",
                  "composition"
                ],
                [
                  "Bound",
                  "compile time",
                  "runtime"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Template Method trap",
              "text": "A rigid, ==deep inheritance hierarchy==. Need runtime swapping? Use Strategy."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Observer, Command and Mediator-Free Messaging",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Observer, Command and Mediator-Free Messaging",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Observer",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Subject** keeps a list of ==observers==",
                "`subscribe` / `unsubscribe` / `notify()` on change",
                "One-to-many, ==loosely coupled==",
                "DOM `addEventListener`, Redux `subscribe`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const off = store.subscribe(render)",
                "// later",
                "off()"
              ],
              "note": "subscribe returns the unsubscribe function"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Forgotten unsubscribe: ==lapsed listener==, memory leak",
                "Notification ==order== is not guaranteed",
                "Cascading updates can ==loop=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Command",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Request as an object with `execute()` and `undo()`",
                "Holds the ==receiver== and its arguments",
                "Enables ==queues==, logging, macros, undo/redo, retry",
                "Examples: editor actions, job queue"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Telling Them Apart",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Observer",
                "Command",
                "Strategy"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Says",
                  "something happened",
                  "do this",
                  "how to do the job"
                ],
                [
                  "Goes to",
                  "many unknown listeners",
                  "one receiver",
                  "its context"
                ],
                [
                  "Receiver",
                  "no",
                  "**yes**",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "Stored, replayed",
                  "no",
                  "**yes**, often undoable",
                  "no"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Observer = ==announce==. Command = ==order==. Strategy = ==method==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Iterator and Chain of Responsibility",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Iterator and Chain of Responsibility",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Iterator",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Iterator== = sequential access, structure stays hidden",
                "`next`/`hasNext`, Python `__iter__`/`__next__`, JS `Symbol.iterator`, generators",
                "One cursor per iterator, so ==independent traversals=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Modify while iterating: Java `ConcurrentModificationException`, or skipped items",
                "Exhausted iterator cannot be reused: ask for a new one"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Chain of Responsibility",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each handler ==processes== the request or ==passes== it on",
                "Sender does not know which handler acts",
                "Examples: middleware, logging levels, support escalation"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Classic",
                "Middleware"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Who acts",
                  "First handler that handles it, then stop",
                  "Every handler acts, then `next()`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Falls off the end",
              "text": "A request can go unhandled. Add a ==default terminal handler=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Chain vs Command",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Chain",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Intent",
                  "Routes one request to whichever handler can take it",
                  "Packages a request for a known receiver"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "They combine well: commands passed through a handler chain"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choosing the Right Pattern",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing the Right Pattern",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Decision Rules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Question",
                "Pattern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Swappable algorithm?",
                  "==Strategy=="
                ],
                [
                  "Behavior follows lifecycle status?",
                  "==State=="
                ],
                [
                  "Fixed steps, variable parts?",
                  "==Template Method=="
                ],
                [
                  "Many parties react to a change?",
                  "==Observer=="
                ],
                [
                  "Undo, queue or log of actions?",
                  "==Command=="
                ],
                [
                  "Unknown handler picks it up?",
                  "==Chain of Responsibility=="
                ],
                [
                  "Hide traversal?",
                  "==Iterator=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Look-Alikes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pair",
                "Difference"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Strategy / State",
                  "Client picks Strategy; State switches itself"
                ],
                [
                  "Strategy / Template",
                  "Composition (runtime) vs inheritance (compile time)"
                ],
                [
                  "Command / Strategy",
                  "Command has a receiver, often undo; Strategy has neither"
                ],
                [
                  "Observer / Chain",
                  "Observer: all notified; Chain: first handler wins"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Trade-off",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "State for two states: a ==boolean== suffices",
                "Strategy for an algorithm that never changes",
                "Observer where a direct call is clearer",
                "Template Method with a deep inheritance chain"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Variation must be real",
              "text": "Every pattern adds classes and indirection. Apply it at the ==second or third variant==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
